  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "admission",
      "text": "Acceptance into the major: AOI and other CEAS students must have a grade of B or higher in all 100-level mathematics, physics, and chemistry courses required by the major, and an overall GPA of 3.2 with no more than one grade of C+ or lower in any course (waivable by the undergraduate program director). Applications are due January 5 (Spring) and June 5 (Fall). Non-CEAS students and double major applicants are admitted competitively, subject to program capacity."
    },
    {
      "topic": "advising",
      "text": "The program culminates in a senior thesis (CME 420) defended at the end of the senior year. Specializations are selected in consultation with a program director by the Spring semester of the junior year."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "Students admitted prior to Fall 2012 complete four (not three) courses in their specialization and four (not three) technical electives at the 300 level or higher."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The accelerated B.E./M.S. program in chemical and molecular engineering allows up to six graduate credits to count toward both degrees. See the Graduate Catalog for requirements."
    },
    {
      "topic": "sbc",
      "text": "In the sample sequence, CME 440 and CME 441 partially satisfy ESI, CER, SPK, WRTD, SBS+, STEM+, and EXP+. CME 441 is a senior design course; contact the CEAS Undergraduate Student Office for details."
    }
  ],
